    "H2 gas phase"
   ],
   "corrections": [],
   "notes": "This is a fully chemically-defined minimal medium spelled out completely in the paper's Materials and Methods; there is no cited base medium, no named trace/vitamin stock to expand, and the only vitamin is calcium pantothenate. The N2-fixing variant is identical to the ammonia-replete medium except the 1 g/L (NH4)2SO4 is replaced by 0.2 g/L anhydrous MgSO4 and nitrogen comes solely from N2 gas. Ion-level exchange components in the target were already complete (Ca, Cl, Fe, glucose, K, Mg, Mo, Na, Pi, pantothenate, sulfate; correctly no ammonium)."
  },
